    <!-- http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.loc.gov/premis/rdf/v3/Identifier"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.loc.gov/premis/rdf/v3/Signature"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>rdf:value is an instance of rdf:Property that may be used in describing structured values.

rdf:value has no meaning on its own. It is provided as a piece of vocabulary that may be used in idioms such as illustrated in example below:

Example 1
&lt;http://www.example.com/2002/04/products#item10245&gt;
    &lt;http://www.example.org/terms/weight&gt; [
       rdf:value 2.4 ;
       &lt;http://www.example.org/terms/units&gt; &lt;http://www.example.org/units/kilograms&gt;
       ] .
Despite the lack of formal specification of the meaning of this property, there is value in defining it to encourage the use of a common idiom in examples of this kind.

The rdfs:domain of rdf:value is rdfs:Resource. The rdfs:range of rdf:value is rdfs:Resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-schema/#ch_value</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <rdfs:label>rdf:value</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


